Kev 0.6B Q4F16 model and ONNX conversion

The runtime route uses onnx-community/kev-0.6b-ONNX at revision
5a827091b3d58fe4fdfc02a5a5b2ce364047d678. The pinned ONNX card declares
Apache-2.0 and describes a conversion of jaredpalmer/kev-0.6b; it names the
source repository but does not state a source commit. For this integration,
the Kev source checkpoint and card are pinned to revision
dece6dba8d43f0f7ded45e9f5b9df12474d90843. The pinned Kev card declares
Apache-2.0 for its adapter and head and identifies Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B-Base as
the base model.

The exact Qwen base revision, da87bfb608c14b7cf20ba1ce41287e8de496c0cd, is
recorded in `training_config.json` at the pinned Kev revision above. This
revision pin comes from that training configuration; the model card itself
names the Qwen repository without a commit hash. The pinned Qwen `LICENSE`
declares Apache-2.0 and includes Copyright 2024 Alibaba Cloud. Its exact text
is included in this package at
`assets/kev06-stable/notices/MODEL-APACHE-2.0.txt`.

The stable `modelId` route has no `assetsUrl` override: the model WASM and
small tokenizer/config/cache metadata are bundled in a lazy JavaScript chunk,
and the pinned ONNX external-data file is fetched from the immutable upstream
revision, reconstructed into TVM shards, and verified before use. The raw ONNX
external-data file is not cached. The notice files are outside the inference manifest and
are not fetched or checked by the browser loader. The JavaScript API/input code
attribution is documented separately in `KEV-NOTICE`.

The pinned Kev card lists ten training data sources and says those datasets
have their own licenses. These cards and notices record upstream declarations
and local file provenance; they do not determine terms for source data,
generated training records, transformed weights, or a particular hosting use.

